id: pm-brief-nd0k
title: Surface pending field-aware merge-decision receipts in pm brief
description: "When the field-aware merge driver discards a peer agent's scalar edit during a merge, the decision is recorded as a pending receipt in .git/pm-merge-receipts, but pm validate reports ok:true and never mentions it (unbraind/pm-cli#770) — so an agent resuming after a merge loads a context that silently omits the peer's work. This feature surfaces pending receipts in brief / brief prompt / brief diverge: compromised items get an inline ⚠ merge marker in focus/next, a dedicated ## ⚠ Pending Merge Decisions section lists the discarded field/value, and brief diverge adds pm merge reconcile to recommended next steps. Receipts are read via @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/merge; each receipt item_path has its stray wrapping single-quote layer stripped (unbraind/pm-cli#771 — Git wraps the %P path). The common case (no pending receipts) stays silent."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T14:45:20.166Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T16:55:06.402Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T16:05:24.612Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "pm brief and pm brief diverge surface pending merge-decision receipts collected from real receipts with item id, conflicting fields and the truncated discarded value; the affected item carries a cross-reference marker; a clean workspace adds no output; the upstream 771 quoted item_path is normalized and never leaks; pm brief --json emits parseable JSON via the host-owned global while an explicit --format wins; 151 tests pass with zero any."
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T16:05:22.131Z",claude-code,"Verified by claude-code with a production proof rather than trusting the unit tests: built extension installed into a throwaway workspace with a REAL two-branch conflicting merge. The collection path correctly maps the real receipt — brief --json reports mergeDecisions.pendingCount 1 with itemId, the normalized itemPath .agents/pm/tasks/<id>.toon carrying no quotes per upstream 771, preferred ours, and conflicts[].discarded holding the peer value. brief diverge --json carries the same section, the cross-reference marker renders as a leading warn merge <id> on the affected item, and a clean workspace adds zero merge-decision output."
  "2026-07-27T16:05:22.647Z",claude-code,"Found and fixed a PRE-EXISTING defect while proving this feature: pm brief --json returned MARKDOWN. The handler read --json from ctx.options, but --json is a host-owned global the CLI consumes into ctx.global, so the check never matched and pm brief --json piped to jq failed on a parse error at the # pm brief heading. Confirmed pre-existing by rebuilding origin/main and reproducing. Fixed by a resolveBriefFormat helper applied at all six format-resolution sites; an explicit --format still wins in both directions. Not a regression from this branch but fixed here because it is the same output path and it is what makes the new merge-decision data reachable through pm's universal convention."
  "2026-07-27T16:05:23.231Z",claude-code,"One pre-existing test had to state its intent explicitly: the SDK test harness defaults globals to json true quiet true noPager true, so a test asserting MARKDOWN was previously passing only because the handler ignored the global. It now passes global json false. Added a contract test pinning the fix, falsification-checked: reverting the helper to the options-only read fails it (150 pass 1 fail) and restoring passes (151 pass 0 fail)."
  "2026-07-27T16:23:05.538Z",claude-code,"Greptile review on PR 46 found a further real defect by running the divergence harness: on a CLEAN divergence (zero changed items) all three non-JSON renderers early-returned before emitting pending receipts, so a discarded peer value was visible only under --format json. That inverts the priority, because a clean divergence is exactly when the dropped value is the ONLY thing worth reporting and markdown is the default. The builder was retaining the receipts correctly and an existing test asserted that, which is why the gap survived: the test covered the builder, not the renderers. Fixed in all three renderers, and the previously DEAD helper mergeDecisionEntryText now has real call sites. Two tests added covering all three formats plus the quiet no-receipt path; falsification verified by reverting the markdown fix (152 pass 1 fail). Suite 153 tests."
  "2026-07-27T16:55:06.401Z",claude-code,"Greptile follow-up review found a residual after the clean-divergence renderer fix: pendingCount carries the TRUE number of pending receipts while receipts is capped at MERGE_DECISION_MAX_RECEIPTS which is 10, so a renderer iterating receipts alone drops the remainder without a word. That is the same silent loss the section exists to surface. Investigation showed the brief's markdown and slack sections ALREADY disclosed it as plus N more, but the agent-prompt path used by brief prompt and by the clean-divergence markdown had NO disclosure at all, and neither did the text or slack clean-divergence paths. Added a shared mergeDecisionOmittedLines helper naming the omitted count and pointing at pm merge report, wired into the agent-prompt renderer and both clean-divergence paths. Four tests added covering all three divergence formats, the brief markdown and slack existing plus-N-more contract, the agent-prompt path, and the negative case where nothing is claimed omitted below the cap. Falsification verified: removing the omission line fails 2 tests (155 pass 2 fail), restoring gives 157 pass 0 fail. Also corrected my own first test here, which asserted the new wording against the brief markdown path that already used a different and pre-existing form."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
